The form was collecting user data but only logging to console. This integrates the Google Sheets web app endpoint to persist submissions directly from the client.

## Changes

**Google Sheets Integration**
- Sends form data (name, email, company, interest, timestamp) via POST with `FormData` and `no-cors` mode
- Handles CORS opacity with 5-second timeout detection to distinguish connection failures from network errors

**Error Handling & UX**
- Specific error messages for timeout vs. network failures
- Proper message state management (prevents success/error from showing simultaneously)
- Accessible error feedback with ARIA attributes (`role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"` for success; `role="alert"`, `aria-live="assertive"` for errors)

**Code Quality**
- Extracted endpoint URL and timeout to `CONFIG` object for maintainability
- Helper functions (`showSuccessMessage()`, `showErrorMessage()`) reduce duplication

## Example

```javascript
// Configuration
const CONFIG = {
    GOOGLE_SHEET_ENDPOINT: 'https://...',
    SUBMISSION_TIMEOUT_MS: 5000
};

// Send with proper error handling
fetch(CONFIG.GOOGLE_SHEET_ENDPOINT, {
    method: 'POST',
    body: formData,
    mode: 'no-cors',
    signal: controller.signal
})
.then(() => showSuccessMessage())
.catch(error => {
    if (error.name === 'AbortError') {
        showErrorMessage('Connection timeout. Please retry.');
    } else {
        showErrorMessage('Network error. Please retry.');
    }
});
```

## Notes

- Server-side validation and rate limiting should be implemented on the Google Apps Script endpoint
- Due to `no-cors` opacity, success message indicates request was sent, not verified receipt

The admin UI had cascading frontend failures: corrupted JS assets (`jszip.min.js`, `core.js`), an invalid chart script include causing 404s, and modal behavior broken by Bootstrap API mismatch. This PR also adds the requested section-based grouping in `admin/users_view.php` so student rows are organized predictably.

- **Users view: add section grouping**
  - Updated query/order flow in `admin/users_view.php` to sort by `section`, then name.
  - Added DataTables draw-time group headers (`Section: ...`) on column 4 (`Section`) for the current page.
  - Normalized empty section labels to `Unassigned` for grouping consistency.

- **Module modal: Bootstrap compatibility fix**
  - Updated modal close button attributes to support both APIs (`data-dismiss` + `data-bs-dismiss`).
  - Added runtime fallback in `admin/module_list.php`:
    - use `bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(...).show()` when available
    - otherwise fall back to `$('#addModuleModal').modal('show')`.

- **Charts/runtime errors: script and asset repair**
  - Removed broken duplicate include `js/chart.min.js` from `admin/footer.php` (source of 404).
  - Replaced corrupted admin assets with known-good in-repo copies:
    - `admin/js/jszip.min.js`
    - `admin/js/core.js`
  - This restores dependent script execution and prevents the syntax/runtime cascade seen in console.

```php
// admin/module_list.php
$('#openAddModuleModal').on('click', function (e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    if (window.bootstrap && bootstrap.Modal) {
        bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(document.getElementById('addModuleModal')).show();
    } else if ($.fn.modal) {
        $('#addModuleModal').modal('show');
    }
});
```
